IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission Act 2014 (NT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL), not the daydate library. The Act's one date a
-- claimant meets is its commencement: 00:01 on 1 January 2015 (endnote 2: s 2 of this Act, s 2(4) of the Territory
-- Insurance Office (Sale) Act 2014 and Gazette S131 of 19 December 2014), the moment the Territory Insurance Office
-- became the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission (s 5(1)) and from which s 43 carries over what was done with TIO.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory; quoted under the NT
-- copyright policy of 8 October 1996 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). This is not an official version of the Act.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Commission Act 2014 (NT)`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- The commencement of the Act: 00:01 on 1 January 2015. A day is the unit here, so 1 January 2015 counts as on or after
-- the commencement (fork F9: the minute from 00:00 to 00:01 is not separated).
`the commencement of the Act` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2015

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `before the commencement of the Act` `the day` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the commencement of the Act`
